WEBVTT

00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:04.280
Summer grasses grow,

00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:05.740
leaving but the dreams of the

00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:07.360
long-gone warriors.

00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:12.130
The dream of unifying Japan was held 
by many lords of the warring states.

00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:15.740
Shingen Takeda.

00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:17.910
Kenshin Uesugi.

00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:20.100
Nobunaga Oda.

00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:25.760
And finally, one man had attained that dream...

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:27.580
Hideyoshi Toyotomi.

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:29.500
Japan had been unified,

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:32.050
and a time of peace appeared to be at hand.

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:34.360
However,

00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:40.720
Hideyoshi's death cast the land 
back into a maelstrom.

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:45.080
With Ieyasu Tokugawa growing 
more influential by the day,

00:00:45.770 --> 00:00:49.150
Mitsunari Ishida tried to prevent his rise to power.

00:00:49.750 --> 00:00:52.280
In order to settle their score once and for all,

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:55.490
the two marched their armies to Sekigahara.

00:00:56.580 --> 00:00:59.870
Kanetsugu Naoe, who'd shared a vow 
of righteousness with Mitsunari,

00:00:59.870 --> 00:01:04.040
tried to lead the Uesugi army 
into battle against Tokugawa.

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:07.670
But the invasion of Masamune Date, 
who had allied himself with Ieyasu,

00:01:07.950 --> 00:01:10.670
meant that Naoe could not get to Sekigahara.

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:16.510
As for the Battle of Sekigahara...

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:20.390
While Mitsunari's Western Army had 
the upper hand in the early going,

00:01:21.050 --> 00:01:23.420
gradually, the tides turned.

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:26.020
In the end, Mitsunari was defeated by Ieyasu,

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:28.850
losing his life.

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:06.870
<i>Episode 5</i>

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:06.870
<i>The Destination of Life</i>

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:12.870
Mitsunari? He lost?

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:26.600
We should retreat.

00:03:27.510 --> 00:03:29.830
I'll handle the rearguard.

00:03:29.830 --> 00:03:30.640
Please hurry!

00:03:33.460 --> 00:03:34.650
Very well.

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:49.200
<i>Mitsunari...</i>

00:03:59.070 --> 00:04:01.170
Once Mitsunari was defeated at Sekigahara

00:04:01.710 --> 00:04:05.430
and Nobuyuki stripped Ueda Castle of its arms,

00:04:05.820 --> 00:04:09.970
Yukimura found himself imprisoned.

00:04:19.540 --> 00:04:20.440
Lord Yukimura,

00:04:21.090 --> 00:04:23.530
look at all the chestnuts I gathered out back.

00:04:24.580 --> 00:04:26.350
They look delicious.

00:04:26.350 --> 00:04:28.990
When we were kids, we used 
to roast them, remember?

00:04:29.870 --> 00:04:34.000
They'd burst all of a sudden, so I burned 
my forehead that one time...

00:04:39.670 --> 00:04:41.030
Uh...

00:04:41.030 --> 00:04:43.760
Oh, some sticky rice would go nicely with them!

00:04:44.070 --> 00:04:46.480
It'll really warm you up!

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:47.760
Yeah.

00:04:48.050 --> 00:04:49.710
Then I'll make some—

00:04:49.710 --> 00:04:51.740
Make some for Tsukimaru.

00:04:52.780 --> 00:04:54.950
Can you eat all this?

00:04:56.270 --> 00:04:58.510
Don't concern yourself with me anymore.

00:04:59.160 --> 00:05:02.200
Tokugawa surely won't keep me alive.

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:02.780
But...

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:05.320
You're free now.

00:05:05.320 --> 00:05:06.670
Live as you please.

00:05:06.670 --> 00:05:07.550
No!

00:05:07.550 --> 00:05:10.030
I'll never leave your side!

00:05:10.290 --> 00:05:13.130
I'm your ninja, after all!

00:05:13.130 --> 00:05:15.340
But soon, I'll be gone.

00:05:16.430 --> 00:05:17.750
No!

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:19.870
If you're going to die, then I'll die with—

00:05:19.870 --> 00:05:20.950
You cannot!

00:05:22.430 --> 00:05:23.980
You cannot die.

00:05:23.980 --> 00:05:25.360
Live on.

00:05:25.870 --> 00:05:27.720
Live your life...

00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:29.800
For yourself this time.

00:05:30.360 --> 00:05:31.410
Understood?

00:05:32.580 --> 00:05:33.560
No!

00:05:44.420 --> 00:05:47.570
Lastly, what shall we do with Yukimura Sanada?

00:05:57.410 --> 00:06:00.710
He has to die! What else?

00:06:01.250 --> 00:06:04.460
Because of him, we suffered so many losses!

00:06:04.770 --> 00:06:06.970
He is not to be underestimated!

00:06:09.390 --> 00:06:10.970
If I may...

00:06:12.190 --> 00:06:17.620
I've heard that the battle at 
Ueda was started by you.

00:06:18.750 --> 00:06:22.730
You fought a pointless battle and, as a result, 
didn't make it to Sekigahara on time.

00:06:22.730 --> 00:06:26.010
Don't you think you are to blame for all of that?

00:06:26.010 --> 00:06:27.740
Shut up, Tadakatsu!

00:06:28.350 --> 00:06:32.400
Yukimura conspired with Mitsunari 
and hindered our advance!

00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:36.700
Lord Hidetada ignored our 
repeated pleas to reconsider,

00:06:36.700 --> 00:06:38.500
and ordered the siege of Ueda Castle.

00:06:38.940 --> 00:06:41.500
Of course a warrior will fight back when attacked!

00:06:42.260 --> 00:06:46.280
Furthermore, Yukimura didn't head to Sekigahara,

00:06:46.280 --> 00:06:48.560
but stayed at Ueda instead.

00:06:48.560 --> 00:06:51.510
How can we say for sure that 
he was allied with Mitsunari?

00:06:52.140 --> 00:06:53.510
Lord Tadakatsu,

00:06:54.040 --> 00:06:56.260
you're being pedantic.

00:06:57.250 --> 00:07:00.120
Yukimura Sanada defeated Lord Hidetada's forces,

00:07:00.590 --> 00:07:03.270
even though they outnumbered his tenfold.

00:07:03.710 --> 00:07:06.150
He is too dangerous to be left alive.

00:07:06.150 --> 00:07:06.780
Oh?

00:07:07.130 --> 00:07:08.540
That's right!

00:07:08.540 --> 00:07:12.530
Besides, we only lost because 
we had a traitor in our ranks!

00:07:12.920 --> 00:07:13.440
Huh?

00:07:13.440 --> 00:07:14.530
A traitor?

00:07:15.460 --> 00:07:16.700
I mean Nobuyuki!

00:07:16.700 --> 00:07:18.920
He conspired with his little brother!

00:07:18.920 --> 00:07:22.120
How else could he have planned those ambushes?

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:24.540
What are you saying?

00:07:25.110 --> 00:07:29.300
Did he not save your life again and again?

00:07:29.860 --> 00:07:31.050
My lord...

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:34.690
Have mercy, if only as a reward 
for Nobuyuki's efforts.

00:07:35.270 --> 00:07:36.300
Please!

00:07:37.740 --> 00:07:39.310
We beg of you!

00:07:43.720 --> 00:07:45.530
F-Father!

00:07:45.530 --> 00:07:47.560
You mustn't be swayed by their words!

00:07:49.310 --> 00:07:52.750
Nobuyuki, what do you think?

00:07:53.400 --> 00:07:54.320
I...

00:08:07.130 --> 00:08:10.590
I believe that even the death penalty 
would be understandable.

00:08:17.480 --> 00:08:18.700
Very well.

00:08:19.870 --> 00:08:24.020
My lord, lots of people left to join you.

00:08:25.770 --> 00:08:28.960
I bet you're trying to run from 
that boy's scolding right now.

00:08:29.360 --> 00:08:31.390
Things may be livelier on your end,

00:08:32.590 --> 00:08:34.830
but I admit I'm a little sad here.

00:08:42.800 --> 00:08:43.860
Is this...

00:08:47.380 --> 00:08:48.840
Mitsunari...

00:08:54.930 --> 00:08:56.890
Lord Mitsunari lost?

00:08:57.770 --> 00:09:00.890
What will happen to the Toyotomi clan now?

00:09:01.990 --> 00:09:03.390
It's all over!

00:09:05.590 --> 00:09:07.230
Lady Kai!

00:09:09.560 --> 00:09:12.280
What is it? You're being awfully noisy.

00:09:12.530 --> 00:09:15.630
What should we do?

00:09:15.630 --> 00:09:18.090
I hear Tokugawa could attack the 
castle as soon as tomorrow.

00:09:18.090 --> 00:09:19.780
Calm down!

00:09:20.350 --> 00:09:25.330
Not even the Tokugawa clan could 
attack Osaka Castle that easily.

00:09:25.330 --> 00:09:26.770
But...

00:09:26.770 --> 00:09:29.150
Lord Hideyori's here, too.

00:09:29.490 --> 00:09:30.810
So relax.

00:09:31.420 --> 00:09:32.090
Okay.

00:09:33.600 --> 00:09:37.740
Kai, who had fought Yukimura's 
group at Odawara Castle,

00:09:37.740 --> 00:09:42.560
was now at Osaka Castle, following the 
Toyotomi clan's suppression of the Hojo.

00:09:49.100 --> 00:09:51.020
I knew you'd be here,

00:09:51.670 --> 00:09:53.030
Lord Hideyori.

00:09:54.850 --> 00:09:56.300
Hey, Kai.

00:09:56.300 --> 00:09:57.510
What's the matter?

00:09:57.900 --> 00:10:03.080
Hideyori Toyotomi

00:09:57.980 --> 00:09:59.250
Following Hideyoshi's death,

00:09:59.250 --> 00:10:03.080
Hideyori had become head of the Toyotomi clan.

00:10:04.390 --> 00:10:07.080
The people in the castle are anxious.

00:10:07.600 --> 00:10:11.590
If you reassured them, they'd feel better.

00:10:12.060 --> 00:10:14.190
Anxious? Why?

00:10:14.190 --> 00:10:16.240
Well, Mitsunari was defeated—

00:10:16.240 --> 00:10:19.740
And the victorious Tokugawa might 
come for the Toyotomi clan next?

00:10:19.740 --> 00:10:21.850
I wouldn't go that far...

00:10:22.850 --> 00:10:25.350
Even the Tokugawa are but vassals 
of the Toyotomi clan.

00:10:26.490 --> 00:10:28.370
Nothing has changed on that end.

00:10:30.430 --> 00:10:32.610
Only the seasons change.

00:10:33.220 --> 00:10:35.960
Seems the season of these 
flowers is coming to a close.

00:10:35.960 --> 00:10:36.440
Wha?

00:10:43.260 --> 00:10:45.570
<i>That smile ought to be outlawed!</i>

00:11:12.930 --> 00:11:14.840
I shall now pronounce your sentence.

00:11:19.640 --> 00:11:21.530
Yukimura Sanada...

00:11:22.140 --> 00:11:23.830
You are hereby sentenced to relegation in Mt. Koya.

00:11:24.410 --> 00:11:26.410
You are to stay rooted in Kudoyama.

00:11:27.480 --> 00:11:29.460
"Mt. Koya relegation."

00:11:29.000 --> 00:11:32.790
Mt. Koya Relegation

00:11:29.460 --> 00:11:32.790
In other words, exile to Mt. Koya.

00:11:33.250 --> 00:11:37.070
"Rooting" meant confinement to a 
home or other designated place,

00:11:34.330 --> 00:11:38.050
Root

00:11:37.070 --> 00:11:39.320
essentially under house arrest.

00:11:40.580 --> 00:11:41.750
Confinement?

00:11:42.150 --> 00:11:43.550
Not death?

00:11:45.860 --> 00:11:46.820
Why?!

00:11:46.820 --> 00:11:50.560
I fought the Tokugawa alongside Lord Mitsunari!

00:11:50.840 --> 00:11:54.650
I don't believe for a second that Lord 
Ieyasu would keep me alive!

00:11:56.360 --> 00:11:57.340
Brother...

00:11:57.730 --> 00:11:59.820
Don't tell me you begged for my life!

00:12:01.510 --> 00:12:02.830
I did not.

00:12:03.540 --> 00:12:04.600
I...

00:12:08.660 --> 00:12:12.080
I believe that even the death penalty 
would be understandable.

00:12:15.260 --> 00:12:16.460
Very well.

00:12:17.230 --> 00:12:18.840
Yukimura Sanada

00:12:20.820 --> 00:12:23.010
is hereby sentenced to Mt. Koya relegation.

00:12:26.360 --> 00:12:27.260
Seriously?

00:12:30.530 --> 00:12:32.000
What?

00:12:32.000 --> 00:12:33.640
Why, Father?

00:12:33.640 --> 00:12:35.600
That man's too dangerous to be left alive—

00:12:35.600 --> 00:12:36.500
Quiet!

00:12:38.500 --> 00:12:42.500
Being late to a battle is a 
warrior's greatest shame!

00:12:42.500 --> 00:12:45.880
Frankly, I'm amazed you 
have the gall to be here!

00:12:45.880 --> 00:12:47.160
B-But...

00:12:47.160 --> 00:12:48.220
Hidetada,

00:12:48.630 --> 00:12:50.790
you are to stay under house arrest for a while, too.

00:12:51.040 --> 00:12:52.250
What?

00:12:52.250 --> 00:12:53.540
Father!

00:12:54.660 --> 00:12:56.040
Understood?

00:12:56.390 --> 00:12:57.900
Yes, sir!

00:12:58.370 --> 00:12:59.540
Nobuyuki...

00:13:00.180 --> 00:13:04.290
Inform Yukimura of his sentence yourself.

00:13:04.290 --> 00:13:05.140
Yes, sir!

00:13:08.190 --> 00:13:10.520
The only reason you escaped the death penalty

00:13:10.520 --> 00:13:13.460
was because Lord Ieyasu is a benevolent man.

00:13:13.460 --> 00:13:14.980
That can't be...

00:13:16.860 --> 00:13:19.540
For my enemy to have mercy on me...

00:13:19.540 --> 00:13:21.980
I have never felt so pathetic!

00:13:24.000 --> 00:13:28.990
Are you telling me to live 
with this shame, Brother?

00:13:29.910 --> 00:13:30.990
That's right.

00:13:31.150 --> 00:13:35.250
If I were to shamelessly live on, 
I couldn't face Lord Mitsunari!

00:13:35.540 --> 00:13:38.090
In that case, I shall take my own life—

00:13:38.090 --> 00:13:39.260
You fool!

00:13:40.820 --> 00:13:44.000
It's fine to consider living shameful.

00:13:44.000 --> 00:13:47.010
However, you should also consider 
why you were kept alive.

00:13:48.070 --> 00:13:50.680
Why I was kept alive?

00:13:50.680 --> 00:13:51.510
Yes.

00:13:51.820 --> 00:13:54.250
What it means for you to stay in this world.

00:13:54.250 --> 00:13:57.270
Reconsider the meaning of your life.

00:13:57.650 --> 00:14:01.180
From here on, Ueda and Numata are 
going to be part of my domain.

00:14:01.640 --> 00:14:04.050
I shall protect the Sanada clan.

00:14:04.810 --> 00:14:08.070
From now on, your duty is to live.

00:14:08.070 --> 00:14:11.370
I won't forgive suicide!

00:14:12.070 --> 00:14:13.710
To live on...

00:14:15.230 --> 00:14:17.550
In due time, I'll tell you when to leave.

00:14:18.020 --> 00:14:19.910
Until then, stay in one place.

00:14:29.330 --> 00:14:33.680
There's no way I can live with this!

00:14:33.680 --> 00:14:35.140
Live on.

00:14:37.420 --> 00:14:40.310
Remember what you said before?

00:14:40.580 --> 00:14:41.910
You told me to live on...

00:14:42.380 --> 00:14:44.900
To live for myself.

00:14:44.900 --> 00:14:46.090
So...

00:14:47.030 --> 00:14:48.810
Please...

00:14:49.590 --> 00:14:50.320
You must live on, too.

00:15:17.440 --> 00:15:18.990
Let's build a castle here.

00:15:18.990 --> 00:15:21.020
Yes, Brother!

00:15:21.930 --> 00:15:23.850
It'll be the Sanada clan's new home.

00:15:26.200 --> 00:15:27.640
So you were here.

00:15:32.310 --> 00:15:36.010
I'm really glad Yukimura escaped execution.

00:15:37.160 --> 00:15:38.770
Do you find me cold-hearted?

00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:43.540
For saying the death penalty 
would be understandable?

00:15:45.550 --> 00:15:48.360
I know how you really feel.

00:15:48.840 --> 00:15:50.960
If you were swayed by love for your brother,

00:15:50.960 --> 00:15:53.050
you would lose your standing 
among the Tokugawa clan.

00:15:54.060 --> 00:15:58.350
You made that painful choice in order 
to protect the Sanada clan, right?

00:15:59.810 --> 00:16:02.270
You told me before that you wanted

00:16:02.670 --> 00:16:04.480
to become the Sanada clan's pillar...

00:16:04.480 --> 00:16:06.560
One that would never crumble.

00:16:07.220 --> 00:16:09.840
And you stuck to that all the way.

00:16:12.290 --> 00:16:14.320
In truth, I wanted to risk it all

00:16:14.730 --> 00:16:17.820
and plead for Yukimura's life.

00:16:18.600 --> 00:16:21.430
But such spinelessness has no place

00:16:21.430 --> 00:16:23.890
in the mission to create a peaceful world.

00:16:24.900 --> 00:16:27.090
It's because I believed in Lord Ieyasu's ideals

00:16:28.040 --> 00:16:31.320
that I chose to serve the Tokugawa clan.

00:16:33.440 --> 00:16:37.910
Still, I might regret those words 
for the rest of my life!

00:16:38.620 --> 00:16:42.600
I... I abandoned my own brother!

00:16:44.040 --> 00:16:45.270
No...

00:16:47.030 --> 00:16:48.430
Lord Nobuyuki!

00:16:59.960 --> 00:17:02.270
Yukimura was only exiled?

00:17:05.150 --> 00:17:06.500
This is pathetic!

00:17:06.930 --> 00:17:08.630
How could I let such a minor wound lay me up?

00:17:09.870 --> 00:17:12.240
If only I'd been there at the council,

00:17:12.670 --> 00:17:14.630
I'd never have let this happen!

00:17:15.500 --> 00:17:16.490
You know...

00:17:16.490 --> 00:17:17.360
Hmm?

00:17:17.790 --> 00:17:20.140
I'm a little relieved, honestly.

00:17:21.370 --> 00:17:23.140
You mean about Yukimura?

00:17:23.420 --> 00:17:24.380
Yeah.

00:17:26.240 --> 00:17:30.020
That guy's just honest to a fault.

00:17:31.330 --> 00:17:34.690
All he did was see his brand of justice through.

00:17:36.550 --> 00:17:39.410
And I'm a bit envious of that.

00:17:42.600 --> 00:17:46.920
Frankly, I did not expect you 
to spare Yukimura's life.

00:17:46.920 --> 00:17:50.380
Why did you want to save him?

00:17:50.720 --> 00:17:53.510
Well, he's my son-in-law's brother.

00:17:53.510 --> 00:17:56.070
Nobuyuki is a fine young man.

00:17:56.530 --> 00:17:59.390
I do not wish to see him sad.

00:18:02.440 --> 00:18:03.430
No.

00:18:03.660 --> 00:18:07.680
Perhaps what I really wanted

00:18:08.200 --> 00:18:10.940
was to fight Yukimura again.

00:18:11.370 --> 00:18:13.890
When I fought him before,

00:18:14.380 --> 00:18:17.700
for the first time in forever, I felt my blood boil.

00:18:18.130 --> 00:18:20.950
The war isn't over yet.

00:18:22.490 --> 00:18:25.300
In order to create a truly peaceful world,

00:18:25.300 --> 00:18:28.570
we must bury the one built on samurai warfare.

00:18:28.940 --> 00:18:31.180
You want to bury the world of the samurai?

00:18:31.570 --> 00:18:32.210
Indeed.

00:18:33.390 --> 00:18:38.600
It must be done in such a way that 
makes it clear to one and all.

00:18:39.320 --> 00:18:40.720
And that

00:18:42.020 --> 00:18:44.470
requires a sacrifice!

00:18:45.740 --> 00:18:48.410
A man that is the very image 
of the samurai spirit.

00:18:49.020 --> 00:18:53.980
His death will be the symbol that marks 
the Warring States Era's end.

00:18:55.130 --> 00:18:58.240
Is that why you're keeping Yukimura alive?

00:18:59.010 --> 00:19:03.130
All for the sake of creating a peaceful world.

00:19:08.400 --> 00:19:09.470
Why?

00:19:09.470 --> 00:19:12.500
Why must I suffer so?!

00:19:13.950 --> 00:19:15.020
It's the Sanada...

00:19:15.020 --> 00:19:16.910
It's all the Sanada clan's fault!

00:19:16.910 --> 00:19:17.840
Curse Yukimura!

00:19:17.840 --> 00:19:19.400
Curse Nobuyuki!

00:19:19.400 --> 00:19:22.050
Then wipe them out.

00:19:28.980 --> 00:19:30.600
Your despised foes...

00:19:34.040 --> 00:19:36.200
And those you resent with everything you are...

00:19:36.760 --> 00:19:40.480
I can rid you of all of them.

00:19:51.750 --> 00:19:53.580
Brother, Sister...

00:19:54.070 --> 00:19:55.280
This is goodbye.

00:19:55.740 --> 00:19:57.770
Live on, Yukimura.

00:19:57.770 --> 00:19:58.760
Understand?

00:20:02.960 --> 00:20:05.330
Please take care of this cherry tree.

00:20:07.390 --> 00:20:08.510
I shall be on my way, then.

00:20:12.840 --> 00:20:13.770
Yukimura...

00:20:17.790 --> 00:20:19.030
Lord Yukimura!

00:20:19.030 --> 00:20:20.900
Let me come with you!

00:20:20.900 --> 00:20:22.320
I'll follow you!

00:20:22.320 --> 00:20:23.310
Please take me with you!

00:20:23.310 --> 00:20:24.090
Lord Yukimura!

00:20:24.090 --> 00:20:24.780
No.

00:20:25.150 --> 00:20:26.260
But why?

00:20:26.260 --> 00:20:29.000
We always have, and always will be, your servants!

00:20:29.000 --> 00:20:30.160
That's right!

00:20:30.160 --> 00:20:31.440
Lord Yukimura!

00:20:31.440 --> 00:20:33.650
Listen up, men.

00:20:33.650 --> 00:20:34.870
From here on,

00:20:34.870 --> 00:20:37.390
my brother, Nobuyuki, will be Ueda's lord.

00:20:39.550 --> 00:20:41.050
These are my final orders.

00:20:41.740 --> 00:20:43.360
You are all to remain in Ueda

00:20:43.360 --> 00:20:46.610
and protect the Sanada clan, under my brother.

00:20:46.610 --> 00:20:47.570
Understood?

00:20:48.100 --> 00:20:49.060
But...

00:20:49.550 --> 00:20:50.810
Understood?

00:20:51.900 --> 00:20:52.560
Y-Yes, sir!

00:20:54.230 --> 00:20:56.120
I wish you all good health.

00:21:02.520 --> 00:21:05.150
<i>I'll follow you anywhere.</i>

00:21:05.150 --> 00:21:08.060
<i>I'm your ninja, after all.</i>

00:21:10.490 --> 00:21:12.780
<i>Take care of Yukimura.</i>

00:21:37.770 --> 00:21:41.360
Yukimura!

00:23:16.120 --> 00:23:20.500
Soon after, Ieyasu Tokugawa received

00:23:20.510 --> 00:23:23.600
the title of shogun.

00:23:34.050 --> 00:23:37.060
He's pretty good, that Ieyasu...

00:23:41.890 --> 00:23:45.150
Sengoku Musou 
High School

00:23:41.890 --> 00:23:45.150
5th Period

00:23:48.060 --> 00:23:48.900
Munch, munch.

00:23:51.180 --> 00:23:54.240
Today, Sister packed me lunch again.

00:23:54.240 --> 00:23:56.070
I wonder what's in it!

00:23:56.780 --> 00:23:59.410
Nobuyuki

00:23:59.900 --> 00:24:01.340
It's love!

00:24:01.340 --> 00:24:04.580
Sister, you got the wrong bag!

00:24:04.580 --> 00:24:05.920
Class 3-A

00:24:06.710 --> 00:24:08.920
What's for lunch today?

00:24:08.920 --> 00:24:09.880
<i>To Be Continued</i>

00:24:09.880 --> 00:24:24.840
<i>Next Episode</i>

00:24:10.620 --> 00:24:13.300
The story takes place in Aizu and Kudoyama.

00:24:13.300 --> 00:24:14.930
Nobuyuki goes to face the Uesugi clan,

00:24:14.930 --> 00:24:16.760
who are considered hostile.

00:24:17.220 --> 00:24:19.560
And Yukimura, who has lost his way of life.

00:24:19.560 --> 00:24:22.310
The wheel of fate turns for the brothers once more.

00:24:21.850 --> 00:24:24.840
<i>Episode Six 
The Caged Heart</i>

00:24:22.310 --> 00:24:24.500
Next time: "The Caged Heart."
